51,39,112,27],[12421,23.9,1951,42,109,24]],"links":[["Edwards County in the Farmland Atlas","/farmland-atlas/texas/edwards-county"],["PRF calculator","/prf"]],"story":"<p class=\"prf-lede prf-story\">As of Oct 12, the record for Edwards County runs 75 years, 1951 to 2025, on the middle value of the county&rsquo;s 15 grids. October to November came in under 90% of normal in 43 of those years, the most of any pair. In 2025, February to March hit 29% of normal and June to July hit 244%. Every grid shown had its driest year in 1956, with grid 11818 down to 25%.</p>"}
